4. Transliteration: Tanzil en.transliteration
==============================================================================

Source:   https://tanzil.net/trans/?transID=en.transliteration&type=txt-2
          (header "Last Update: September 6, 2010"), kept verbatim in
          data/tanzil/en.transliteration.txt.
Author:   not named. Tanzil lists the translator as "English Transliteration";
          no person or publisher is given.
Terms:    only Tanzil's translation terms apply: "for non-commercial purposes
          only". Because no rights holder is named, permission for any other
          use cannot be requested.

This text is NOT clearly redistributable beyond non-commercial use. It is kept
as an interim choice while the project is non-commercial, because it is the
only transliteration that can be pinned and verified like the Arabic: the
Quran Foundation API may not be cached or bundled, and a transliteration
generated from the Arabic would be machine-made text that nobody has checked.
Before any commercial use, replace it or obtain clear permission (tracked in
REVIEW.md). data/quran.json removes the file's inline HTML markup (<u>, <b>,
<i>, <strong>) and changes nothing else.

